{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested on exact head 363a24ae5cf4c13b6df93e127a95a689350d6bb3. The high-level conclusion is sound: do not rewrite workroom in JSONata; first preserve an executable oracle, then expose commitment closure as data, and keep authority/admission native. The measured claims I sampled reproduce: exact clean pushed sole-path head on e2c29034; fold.go 3,565 lines/108 functions; workroom 200 tests; 58 fold-touching commits; 20 profile-version commits; the six longest spans; 36 literal refusal reasons and 47 Decision constructions. `make docs`, `go test ./internal/workroom -count=1`, and diff checks pass. Current main a30406b3 advances only the disjoint querysandbox README/test paths, so the cited source basis remains current for this note.\n\nArchitecture: research-only notes touch no runtime layer or published contract. The recommended stable Go kernel and fixed authority boundary preserve architecture layer 5 and correctly avoid adding SQLite/JSONata/runtime identity to workroom without a deletion win. Five design corrections are required before this can safely govern follow-on work. (1) The text alternates between a temporal transition machine and the actual final-fact-to-status decision function. `projectCommitments` has no prior-state input. Define which model is proposed. An ordered first-match table permits overlapping guards, while §5.4's “exactly one row matches” requires mutually exclusive guards and makes ordering semantically irrelevant. Pick one and specify the corresponding completeness, overlap and reachability tests. (2) S0 has no second implementation to compare. Specify the preserved oracle/frozen projection or candidate interface, its full-history input, how later candidates plug in, and a deliberately perturbed candidate that proves the harness detects a difference. Comparing the current reducer to itself is not a gate. (3) Retirement involution cannot restore every projected field: the supersession acts remain in Statements, Decisions and Provenance. Scope the property precisely to retirement-dependent semantic rows/fields. (4) A generator of only legal act sequences cannot exercise the refusal branches the live corpus lacks. Include deterministically bounded malformed payloads, schema-valid but semantically invalid acts, invalid bases, departed/unauthorized actors, duplicate IDs, redefinitions, and receipt/accounting adversaries, with an oracle for the expected invariant rather than undefined behavior. (5) Option C is not general workflow generation. It is configurable commitment-status policy over a closed host fact vocabulary; novel speech acts, facts, multi-party approvals, authority rules, and merge semantics still require host code and a profile change. State that limit and give at least two concrete workflows the proposed declaration can and cannot express.\n\nSecurity: the exact head executes nothing and introduces no direct vulnerability. Its non-declarable authority boundary and rejection of executable JSONata policy are good. Approval is blocked because the legal-only generator and undefined S0 oracle would leave authority/refusal regressions outside the promised safety case.\n\nSimplification: the no-big-bang and no-workroom-Tailapps recommendations are supported, and the honest deletion budget is valuable. Approval is blocked because calling an overlapping decision cascade a fully enumerable transition machine hides rather than exposes its semantics. Resolve the five points without expanding scope; retain the measured evidence, migration stages, observability, performance gates, and Tailapps conclusion.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:f35b109e98faa903c67e0f4779aca40c088037f3","head":"363a24ae5cf4c13b6df93e127a95a689350d6bb3","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:df6484c1558ce21f7bcbc8de6bf74386a25bc822\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0b